What is an I.P. Address?
It is Internet Protocol addresses and it is used to identify other locations and computers.

Why is Tim Breners-Lee important?
He invented the World Wide Web.

What is the last mile?
The last mile is what connects homes and smaller places to the internet.

What does the lock next to a url signify?
It means that the connection between the browser and server is encrypted so no one else can see it.

What is the IETF, what does it do?
The IETF is the Internet Engineering Task Force and they make the internet work by organizing and creating standards for how it should run.

What is ICANN, what does it do?
It is the Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers and it gives out domain names and IP addresses.

What is a packet?
It is a virtual envelope with specific information, like the IP address, about the request when you do something.

Why are websites broken up and transmitted in small pieces?
They are broken up so they can pass through a place that has a smaller transmission unit than the original and it is also faster and more efficient.
